<article class="env-lemma" id="0BXI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BXI">Lemma <span data-tag="0BXI">31.16.10</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian UFD. Let $I \subset R$ be an ideal such that $R/I$ has no embedded primes and such that every minimal prime over $I$ has height $1$. Then $I = (f)$ for some $f \in R$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0BXH" data-tag="0BXH">31.16.9</a> the ideal sheaf $\tilde I$ is invertible on $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$. By More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BCH" data-tag="0BCH">15.119.3</a> it is generated by a single element. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>